WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.569
- There is one place where

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.071
it's rewarded, the poker table.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.240
A poker player can win if
they have the best hand,

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.009
or if they convince the
other players that they do.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.878
But even when
someone is bluffing,

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:14.280
their body language
may give them away.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.648
[music playing]

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:18.084
The smallest involuntary
movements in our face

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:21.521
are amazingly accurate
windows into our feelings.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.290
These are called
micro expressions.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.760
They can last just
1/25th of a second

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:30.196
and express any one of
seven universal emotions,

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.933
fear, anger, sadness,
disgust, happiness,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.269
contempt, and surprise.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:39.105
Micro expressions are almost
impossible to control, which

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:42.542
is why FBI agents will film
interrogations and analyze

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:46.112
the footage to see
if a person is lying.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.914
There are lawyers who
study micro expressions

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.282
during jury selection.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.217
And psychiatrists can
be trained to watch

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.887
for these small movements
in therapy sessions.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.922
If anyone can hide
their micro expressions,

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.292
it's people whose
living depends on it.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.795
So we've invited some of the
planet's best poker players

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.565
to join us for our
next game, including

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:08.268
World Series of Poker
Champion and European

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.737
Tour Champion Liv Boeree.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.838
Hey, Liv, how you doing?

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.639
I'm doing great.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.740
Thanks for coming.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.660
Please welcome Liv
Boeree, Igor Kurganov,

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.900
Wayne Chiang, and Alec Torelli.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.314
[cheers and applause]

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:27.153
These poker pros make a living
reading the micro expressions

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.655
on other people's faces.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:32.058
We're going to see if they can
keep us from seeing theirs.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.259
Here's how it's going to work.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.494
For the first
challenge, there are

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.830
four identical shot glasses.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.031
Two have apple juice.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.999
Two have apple cider vinegar.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.635
After each of you takes
a sip, you have to say,

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.170
this tastes good.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.639
If Ted and I can tell
who's had the juice

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.341
and who's had the
vinegar, we win.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.376
If we can't, you win.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.811
Simple enough?
- All right.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.146
- Yep.
- Do it.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.681
KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY: Let's get
the first round under way.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.116
[music playing]

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.188
This tastes good.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:08.962
This tastes good.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.369
This tastes good.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.338
[laughing]

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.341
Ah.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.780
This tastes good.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.482
Geez, Louise.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.750
OK, all right.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.185
TED DANSON: I'm just going
straight to shame on you.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.554
You just-- [chuckles]
we're both going Wayne.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.755
Yeah.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.790
But we have another person.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.993
Yeah, I think it's
Liv because I think

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.028
she asked for the toxic crap.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:42.829
And--

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.531
Oh, I see.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.698
I see.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.401
Now, I want to say
it's Wayne and Igor.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:49.402
TED DANSON: Right.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:52.772
So it is time to
reveal your cards.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.874
Who had the vinegar,
raise your hand?

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:55.675
Son of a--

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.110
TED DANSON: [laughs]

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:59.412
[applause]

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:04.918
I so-- oh, man,
are you kidding me?

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.019
That's funny.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.888
OK, so our next round,
that you're going to

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:09.689
love this, guys.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:10.757
All right.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:14.260
Our next round is
guacamole versus wasabi.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.763
Oh.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:20.233
[chuckles] So you guys,
let's [shuffling sound]

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.200
shuffle up and taste.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.602
Here we go.

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:25.038
[music playing]

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:27.607
This tastes good.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.008
OK, Igor.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.818
This tastes good.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:39.752
- Wayne.
- Clean.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:40.753
That was clean.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.622
That was a clean
one with the chew.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.091
He was working it.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:46.092
This tastes good.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.126
[chuckling]

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:47.927
KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY:
Oh, see now, he's

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:48.728
going to do that every time.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.796
He's going to make it feel--

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.197
Yeah, he's going to
try to throw us off.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.465
He's going to say, this tastes
good uncomfortably every time.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.836
This tastes good.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.905
KEEGAN-MICHAEL KEY: Oh,
gosh, Ted, this is tough.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.006
- He's good.
- He is good.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:00.740
He's good.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:01.808
I'm not get--

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.710
but now we know that
Wayne's got a thing.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:07.113
He's working baseline
on the vocals.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.514
TED DANSON: Liv's
blinking like crazy.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.582
- Yeah, yeah, look at that.
- I think--

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:10.984
Oh, yeah, there's a
thing going on here.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.719
- --her eyes are watering.
- Just really happy to be here.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.555
She's just-- [laughs]
she's so happy to be here,

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:16.756
it's bringing her to tears.
TED DANSON: Yeah.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.057
[laughs]

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.927
There might be nothing
she could do about that.

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:24.998
OK, blam, I've got
a Liv and a Wayne.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.099
What about you, Ted?

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.533
I got Igor and Liv.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.468
Igor and Liv.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.535
Ted's got Igor and Liv.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:32.772
OK, time again to
show your cards.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.440
Who had the wasabi?

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.842
Ho.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:36.776
